<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To validate the effectiveness of our method, we compare our method with existing structural pruning methods on LLaMA-2-7B model and then evaluate the pruned model on 10 popular zero-shot benchmarks.
The results are listed in Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5.2.1 Comparison of Existing Methods ‣ 5.2 Experimental Results ‣ 5 Experiment ‣ High-Fidelity Pruning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
The results demonstrate that our method significantly outperforms other structural pruning methods, when 20% and 30% parameters of LLaMA-2-7B model are pruned.
When pruning ratio is set to 20%, our method achieves 59% average accuracy over 10 popular zero-shot benchmarks, surpassing the second best method, SDMPrune, by 0.8%.
Notably, our method even outperforms the original model by 0.7%.
We further explore high pruning ratio as 30%, our HFPrune is consistently superior to other methods.
The above results indeed support the superiority of our method on LLM compression task.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">

