<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Implementation Details.</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To restore model performance post-pruning, we conduct a brief fine-tuning phase using the AdamW
optimizer and BF16 precision. As detailed in Table <a href="#A1.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ A.1 Implementation Details. ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ High-Fidelity Pruning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>,
we customized the hyperparameters for each model and sparsity ratio. For instance, larger models
like LLaMA2-7B and Qwen2.5-7B were trained with a larger batch size of 512 on 8<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>A6000 GPUs,
while smaller models used a batch size of 256 on 4<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>4090 GPUs. The learning rates were also adjusted,
ranging from <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> depending on the model scale.</p>
</div>
