</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>More Detailed Evaluation Results</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To complement the summarized results presented in the main body,
this section provides a more granular breakdown of our method’s performance on
the LLaMA-3.2 model series. Table <a href="#A1.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ A.2 More Detailed Evaluation Results ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ High-Fidelity Pruning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> and Table <a href="#A1.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ A.2 More Detailed Evaluation Results ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ High-Fidelity Pruning for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>
present the detailed zero-shot evaluation scores for the LLaMA-3.2-1B and LLaMA-3.2-3B models, respectively.
These tables show the performance across benchmarks,
offering a comprehensive view that reinforces the consistent advantage of our entropy-based
pruning criterion over existing baselines at both 20% and 30% sparsity ratios.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T10" class="ltx_table">
